//Parts of the compiler pipeline (Fused through Codegen) incorrectly expect all
//label uses to have offset 0 into the label and byte length 2.
//That's an obstacle to imported labels (necessary for Sol-style immutable
//variables, dynamic linking), but it's already a bug: a 2-byte label in a
//tag may be shifted across a word boundary.
//This module should trigger that.

import Prelude;

data D = {D};
tag D = Struct(()->(),UInt 31) where {
 D: Struct (main,0) //main will be split over two words
 };
main () := returnValue D